-- title:
--   Lemma 13 — $\mathcal Q_\gamma$ is a soundness profile for fresh-coin arms, and $q_A+q_B\le\varepsilon_{\mathrm{eff}}$ on it
-- statement:
--   Consider a routed run satisfying arm soundness (HA) with errors $\varepsilon_A,\varepsilon_B$, and let $\gamma$ bound its A-forgery rate. Then:
--
--   1. the set $\mathcal Q_\gamma=\{(q_A,q_B):q_A\le g\varepsilon_A,\ q_B\le(1-g)\varepsilon_B\ \text{for some }g\in[0,\gamma]\}$ is a soundness profile of the run;
--   2. every $(q_A,q_B)\in\mathcal Q_\gamma$ satisfies
--   $$
--   q_A+q_B\le\varepsilon_{\mathrm{eff}}:=\varepsilon_B+\gamma(\varepsilon_A-\varepsilon_B)^+ .
--   $$
--
--   The lemma turns the per-arm soundness errors and the forgery rate into a profile to which Theorem 14 applies.
--
--   Differences from the source:
--   - generalization: every prover interacting with the verifier on a false statement → every probability space $(\Omega,\mu)$, every filtration $(\mathcal F_j)$, every family of post-base-stage σ-algebras $\mathcal G_j$ and every adapted run $(\rho,a)$ (`IsRoutedRun`); reason: the run of any prover is such a run, with $\mathcal F_j$ generated by the first $j$ rounds and $\mathcal G_j$ by $\mathcal F_{j-1}$ and $\nu_j$; the theorem specializes to the paper's
--   - encoding: the hypothesis $x\notin L$ → not modelled; reason: the run is the run on a false statement; the hypotheses (H0), (HA) and the forgery bound are what $x\notin L$ supplies
--   - encoding: rounds $j=1,\dots,N$ conditioned on $\mathcal F_{j-1}$, answers $a_j\in\{0,1\}$ → 0-based rounds $j<N$ conditioned on `F j`, answers in `Bool`; reason: relabelling; same instances
--   - encoding: $\mathbb P[S\ge\tau]$ and conditional probabilities $\mathbb P[E\mid\mathcal F]$ almost surely → `μ.real {ω | τ ≤ creditSum …}` and `condProb` (Mathlib `condExp` of the indicator), with `∀ᵐ`; reason: Lean convention; the events are measurable, so these are the paper's quantities
--   - reading: (HA): for every view $\nu$ and prover strategy, $V_X$ accepts $\Pi_X$ on $(x,\nu)$ with probability at most $\varepsilon_X$ → $\mathbb P[a_j=1\mid\mathcal G_j]\le\varepsilon_{\rho_j}$ almost surely in every round $j<N$ (`ArmSound`); reason: p.6 states that by fresh arm coins (HA) holds for every history, and the proof of Lemma 13 uses exactly this conditional form; no model of interactive machines is formalized
--   - generalization: $\gamma=\sup\mathbb P[\rho_j=A\mid\mathcal F_{j-1}]$ over provers, rounds and histories → any real $\gamma$ with $\mathbb P[\rho_j=A\mid\mathcal F_{j-1}]\le\gamma$ almost surely for $j<N$ (`ForgeryBound`); reason: the paper's $\gamma$ is such a bound for every prover's run
--   - reading: $\mathcal Q_\gamma$ printed without the constraint $(q_A,q_B)\in[0,1]^2$ → $\mathcal Q_\gamma\cap[0,1]^2$ (`Qgamma`); reason: Definition 12 requires a soundness profile to be a subset of $[0,1]^2$; the intersection does not change the supremum in Theorem 14
--   - generalization: soundness errors $\varepsilon_A,\varepsilon_B$ and forgery rate $\gamma$ in $[0,1]$ → $\varepsilon_A,\varepsilon_B,\gamma$ arbitrary reals; reason: both conclusions hold for all reals; they specialize to the paper's
-- source:
--   Dumlu, Signal-Routed Two-Arm Verification, STOC 2027 submission manuscript (held version, sha256 d56b3b7a…), Lemma 13, p.7

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_SigRoute_IsProfile
import Definitions.Def_SigRoute_Qgamma
import Definitions.Def_SigRoute_ArmSound

namespace SigRoute

open MeasureTheory

/-- Lemma 13 (Profile for fresh-coin arms) (Dumlu, Signal-Routed Two-Arm Verification, STOC 2027 submission manuscript (held version, sha256 d56b3b7a…), Lemma 13, p.7). Assume (HA). Then
`Q_γ = {(q_A, q_B) : q_A ≤ g ε_A, q_B ≤ (1 − g) ε_B for some g ∈ [0, γ]}` is a soundness profile, and
every `(q_A, q_B) ∈ Q_γ` satisfies `q_A + q_B ≤ ε_eff := ε_B + γ(ε_A − ε_B)⁺`.

**Formalization Note** The paper's "every prover" is "every probability space `(Ω, μ)`, filtration `F`, post-base-stage σ-algebras `G` and adapted run `(ρ, a)`" (`IsRoutedRun`); rounds are 0-based, so the paper's `F_{j−1}` is `F j`. (HA) is its conditional form given the post-base-stage σ-algebra
`G j` (`ArmSound`), and `γ` is any almost-sure bound on `P[ρ_j = A | F_{j−1}]` (`ForgeryBound`). `Q_γ`
is intersected with `[0,1]²` (`Qgamma`). No range is assumed on `ε_A, ε_B, γ`. -/
theorem lemma_13 {Ω : Type*} {m : MeasurableSpace Ω} (μ : Measure Ω)
    [IsProbabilityMeasure μ] (F : Filtration ℕ m) (G : ℕ → MeasurableSpace Ω)
    (ρ : ℕ → Ω → Arm) (a : ℕ → Ω → Bool) (hrun : IsRoutedRun F G ρ a) (N : ℕ)
    (ε : Arm → ℝ) (γ : ℝ) :
    (ArmSound μ G ρ a N ε → ForgeryBound μ F ρ N γ → IsProfile μ F ρ a N (Qgamma ε γ)) ∧
    ∀ q ∈ Qgamma ε γ, q.1 + q.2 ≤ epsEff ε γ := by sorry

end SigRoute
